From c7251d9897e7bd0805d5062ad40971625ad86abf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuanyuan Chen <cyyever@outlook.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 00:23:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] clr: end the capture when hipStreamEndCapture reports
 unjoined work

On hipErrorStreamCaptureUnjoined, hipStreamEndCapture released the
capture graph but left the origin stream and every stream that joined
the capture in the capturing state, and did not clear *pGraph. A later
global-mode check then failed unrelated calls such as hipMalloc, and the
streams could not start a new capture. Clear *pGraph and end the capture
as the invalidated path already does.

develop fixes this as part of a larger rework of capture membership
(#11589).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 projects/clr/hipamd/src/hip_graph.cpp | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/projects/clr/hipamd/src/hip_graph.cpp b/projects/clr/hipamd/src/hip_graph.cpp
index 9692831f85..4af59f2ba1 100644
--- a/projects/clr/hipamd/src/hip_graph.cpp
+++ b/projects/clr/hipamd/src/hip_graph.cpp
@@ -1343,8 +1343,11 @@ hipError_t hipStreamEndCapture_common(hipStream_t stream, hip::Graph** pGraph) {
     s->GetCaptureGraph()->RemoveNode(pGraphNode);
     s->GetCaptureGraph()->RemoveManualNodesDuringCapture();
     if (leafNodes.size() > 1 && foundInRemovedDep == false) {
+      *pGraph = nullptr;
       // Release created graph as it can't be retrieved anymore
       s->ReleaseCaptureGraph();
+      // As for an invalidated capture, return every stream in it to non-capturing
+      (void)s->EndCapture();
       return hipErrorStreamCaptureUnjoined;
     }
   } else {
